 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to home visiting services\nfor applicants for, or recipients of, public assistance benefits who are\nexempt from certain work activities",
    "basePrintNo": "S5810",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5810-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§332, 335, 335-b & 336, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5810\n\nSPONSOR: MONTGOMERY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the social services law, in relation\nto home visiting services for applicants for, or recipients of, public\nassistance benefits who are exempt from certain work activities\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to home visiting\nservices for applicants for, or recipients of, public assistance bene-\nfits who are exempt from certain work activities\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 332 of the social services law by adding new\nsubdivision 1-a:\n1-a. Provides that recipients of public assistance who are exempt from\nwork activities shall be eligible to receive home visiting services\nprovided they otherwise meet eligibility criteria. Provides that local\nsocial services districts shall provide information about home visiting\nservices to applicants for public assistance.\n\n2. This subdivision is amended to provide that reviews of services\noffered to recipients of public assistance include a home visiting where\nit may be beneficial.\n\nParagraph (c) is added to provides to local social services officials\nshall encourage participation in home visitation where appropriate.\nProvides that home visiting activity shall count toward an individual's\nwork requirements.\n\n3. Amends paragraph (c) to ensure parents are provided with information\nthat such home visiting activities count toward a recipient's work\nactivity requirement.\n\n4. Amends paragraphs (f) and (m). Defines job search and job readiness\nassistance to include home visiting programs\n\n5. Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nEvidence-based and evidence-informed home visiting programs provide\nfamilies with services to prevent child abuse and maltreatment, enhance\npositive parent child interactions and empower families to develop and\nachieve their self-sufficiency goals. These critical programs for fami-\nlies provide a host of early intervention services that can assist fami-\nlies and prevent often serious and costly familial and societal prob-\nlems. Applicants for or recipients of public assistance who are exempt\nfrom work activities and have dependent children are required by law to\nreceive an employability assessment that takes into consideration educa-\ntion level, literacy, English language proficiency, child care and other\nsupportive service needs as well as prior work experience, training and\nvocational interests.  This legislation would require a review of family\ncircumstances and the needs of the child/children to determine if home\nvisiting services would be appropriate and beneficial to the family. It\nwould also require an eligible parent or caretaker with a child under\nthe age of five to be provided with information regarding their partic-\nipation in home visiting programs that would both benefit their family\nand partially satisfy their work requirement.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
